00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.280 align:start position:0%
 
hello and welcome to the new world  review your source for everything anime  and manga and today we have a review of  episode 3 of doctor stone weapons of  science and here we are back for another  round of rebuilding civilization and  this week was such an incredibly chilled  episode I felt which is weird especially  considering all the tension that was  generated early on but this is why I  love dr. stone because this series has  such a different focus to a traditional  Shonen and its core it's all about  science and exploration which makes it  real easy to just sit down to and be  swept up in whatever journey or  discovery the characters are working on  for example my favorite part of this  week's episode was probably the whole  section with sanku tied you and you  Zahira we're just traveling and seeing  what they run into like the big buddha  or how they logistically managed past  obstacles but Taichi pulling the rafts  thing and the general day-to-day needs  of simple survival and they also think  that this works a lot better in the  anime than it did in the manga which  don't get me wrong and was still nice  and chill in the manga but sometimes  that can be problematic for me because  reading manga is a bit more of an active  experience your eyes are constantly  moving from panel to panel of various  sizes from text to text which could be  anywhere and your imagination is invoked  for voices sound effects or any  perception of color or anything like  that and it's great fun but for sections  like this it really is nice to just have  the anime take care of everything so  that you can just lie back and enjoy the  journey  and one of the characters on set journey  was our newest addition user hero now we  had already gotten a bit of a sense of  her from the first episode but this week  provided a much better taste of what  she'll have to offer going forward and  I'm pretty satisfied with her I guess  her voice is absolutely lovely and  gellick even but when it comes to use a  hero I have deeper problems with her as  a character and that's because doctors  don't is a series that from time to time  can get the bit ropey with certain  characters and that's very much what  user hero feels like to me I like her  design I now like her voice I just wish  she wasn't such a a classically passive  female presence it's not a huge issue  because this series can get away with  little flaws like that just based on its  actual core focus and what I will say  for user here as a character really is  that she is not in any way annoying  which is often the case for the passive  female presence in anime and manga as we  see in this episode she is quick to get  on board with any sort of shenanigan  area to do with singko and tide you  she's not overly serious and in fact she  for some great comic faces from time to  time I just wish she had a bit more  depth to her and you know going forward  that may become a common criticism I  have for other characters but once again  a series like this can  away with it whereas it would be a  crippling detriment to others so as a  result I'm going to say that the anime  has pulled off user hero more or less as  well as they could have and I am looking  forward to seeing more of her in the  animated medium but a character who  continues to grow on me as a result of  his adaptation is most certainly tied  you in this world of Chill that I claim  to love so much he is a much-needed  burst of energy from time to time that  breaks it all up a bit  I mean think of everyone else we have so  far we've got sanku the called genius  use a hero the softly spoken and Tsukasa  who despite being a vicious murderer is  wildly calm and collected so at the  moment I do feels a very important role  if being a dumb loud idiot and it's  something that I greatly appreciate  being done so well in the adaptation but  there is a lot more to him than that and  we get a taste of his true character  here with his conflict against Tsukasa  and I have to say in the manga tied you  is not a character who really held my  interest at all until this moment but he  declares that he refuses to hit people  and that Tsukasa can beat him up as much  as he wants in exchange for not  destroying the stone folk it's such a  wonderfully endearing idiot sort of  thing to say that I could not help but  love him from that moment on and the  anime has made me revisit this point of  conversion all over again and does per  everything else I've mentioned so far it  was handled really well speaking of that  conflict with Tsukasa though the anime  certainly stepped up this week in terms  of action a major criticism that I had  for last week's episode was that  tsukasa's action sequences felt rather  unfortunately pretty weak due to  animation techniques like throwing a  punch and then immediately cutting to  the results thus lessening the overall  impact however during this episode there  was one fantastically animated moment of  Tsukasa grabbing the shot that Cinco  fired from his crossbow and going on to  strike tied you I loved that I could  really feel tsukasa's momentum from the  shot of his foot pivoting all the way  through the sequence the illusion was  sold pretty damn well not phenomenally  compared to more action-based series but  it certainly got the job done for doctor  stone and it gives me some decent hope  for future events now in terms of action  we had one pretty big goal flag this  week being the creation of firearms and  this also happens to be the primary  difference between the anime and the  manga for this episode specifically when  cenk who chooses to reveal that they're  searching for gunpowder in the manga  cent crew pretty blatantly states that  they need to make gunpowder as soon as  Tsukasa leaves their camp which works  quite well in the context of the chapter  because that's what it ends on and it's  a very exciting note but the decision to  move this revelation in the anime was  certainly the correct course of action  because it gave this episode a similar  effect that the manga originally had and  I don't think you miss a lot from not  knowing that they're adventuring for  gunpowder until much later because you  still have that  motivation to flee because there is that  need to separate themselves from Tsukasa  so it was a nice and probably necessary  change for dramatic purposes something  else I think this episode nailed was the  slew of comic faces that appeared and  this was something and I was a bit  afraid of after watching the first  episode because there were comic faces  in the manga that were removed  specifically of sanku and it had me  worried because I thought they might be  trying to portray him as a much more  serious character than he actually is  this week has put all of that to rest as  the series really is starting to  properly embrace its comic layers also  to do it there's a bad transition but  here we are music once again I'm finding  that the music of this series is superb  and the track that specifically stood  out to me here was the one that played  during the conflict with Tsukasa  it was incredibly effective at building  tension and look I'm pathetic with music  so I'm not sure how to properly put this  into words but it also felt distinctly  tribal it's probably not the right word  at all but it was very effective in  evoking a primitive atmosphere so well  done there sadly in terms of music the  ending theme it still hasn't grown me  whatsoever and they still really hate  the visuals that take place in the real  world with the stupid filter and so I'm  probably going to be skipping it from  here on out the opening however is the  exact opposite I love the energy it  brings and I've been listening to the  full version periodically for a couple  of days now and I am still loving it and  the last thing I'd like to mention is  that this is pretty much the end of  volume 1 which is awesome it took just  three episodes to blast through it had a  very decent pace and vol 2 is where  things really start to kick into gear so  I am very excited for the next few weeks  and I hope that you are as well but that  pretty much does it for episode 3 of dr.  stone if you enjoyed this video and the  content this channel produce in general  then please do consider donating to the  New World review patreon because the  support of all feel amazing people is  what continues to make this channel  possible and if patreon isn't quite your  style then please do leave this video a  like share or subscribe because it also  helps plot this channel an incredible  amount and if you'd like to join the fun  at any time then please do head over to  my discord server where a wide array of  shenanigan ray takes place on a daily  basis and finally please do comment with  your thoughts on the episode this has  been the new old review and I'll see you  next time

